## Phase 1 — Build Performance Attribution

**Goal:** Make P&L explainable.

Right now the platform can report overall outcomes. That is not enough.
We need to know:

* which strategy is working
* on which symbols
* in which regimes
* for what hold period
* at what conviction level
* under which market conditions

## What to Track

### By strategy

* gross P&L
* net P&L
* win rate
* loss rate
* expectancy
* average gain / average loss
* Sharpe-like return score
* max drawdown contribution
* number of trades
* hold duration

### By analyst

* signal hit rate
* realized P&L of trades influenced
* average conviction vs actual outcome
* false-positive rate
* false-negative / missed-opportunity rate when tracked
* cost per analyst run
* value created per $1 of LLM spend

### By symbol

* per-symbol expectancy
* regime-specific profitability
* slippage profile
* volatility-adjusted return contribution

### By setup type

Examples:

* breakout
* earnings gap
* mean reversion
* oversold bounce
* panic selloff
* sector momentum
* macro risk-off fade

Each setup type should have its own statistics.

### By regime

At minimum classify market conditions into:

* trend up / trend down / range
* low vol / medium vol / high vol
* risk on / risk off
* earnings-heavy / macro-heavy / quiet

### By time horizon

* intraday
* 1-day hold
* 2–3 day swing
* multi-day continuation

