## Phase 2 — Create a Common Trade Candidate Schema

**Goal:** Normalize every trade idea into one comparable object.

Today, strategy signals and AI picks are different shapes conceptually.
That makes ranking and capital allocation harder than it should be.

## New Trade Candidate Object

Every idea should become a normalized `TradeCandidate` with fields like:

```ts
interface TradeCandidate {
  candidateId: string
  timestamp: string
  sourceType: 'strategy' | 'ai_panel' | 'event_scanner' | 'copy_trade'
  sourceId: string
  strategyId?: string
  analystIds?: string[]
  symbol: string
  side: 'BUY' | 'SELL'
  setupType: string
  thesis: string
  convictionRaw: number
  expectedHorizon: 'intraday' | 'swing_1d' | 'swing_3d' | 'multi_day'
  regimeSnapshotId: string
  featureVector: Record<string, number | string | boolean>
  estimatedEdge?: number
  estimatedRisk?: number
  estimatedSlippageBps?: number
  supportingSignals: string[]
}
```

## Why this matters

The allocator cannot compare apples to oranges.
This schema makes everything rankable.

### Exit Criteria

All signal paths write into the same candidate pipeline before execution.

