# Metrics That Actually Matter

## Primary Metrics

* expectancy per trade
* profit factor
* max drawdown
* Sharpe proxy
* return on deployed capital
* return by book
* return by strategy
* return by setup

## Secondary Metrics

* win rate
* average hold time
* slippage
* turnover
* candidate-to-trade conversion rate
* AI cost per profitable trade
* analyst calibration quality

## Anti-Metrics

Do not optimize for:

* number of strategies
* number of AI agents
* number of trades
* number of endpoints
* number of “insights” generated

Those are ego metrics.

