# What to Stop Doing

1. Stop adding generic strategies just because they are easy to code
2. Stop treating consensus among LLMs as evidence of edge
3. Stop using flat position sizes once attribution exists
4. Stop mixing incompatible time horizons in one scorecard
5. Stop letting memory act like learning unless it changes decisions
6. Stop promoting anything to live capital without a promotion path

---

# The Real Bet

The real bet is not that OpenClaw Trader will magically predict the market better because it has more models.

The real bet is this:

> If the platform can observe outcomes cleanly, identify where edge actually exists, and allocate capital more intelligently than a static system, it can become materially better over time.

That is the right bet.

Not “more indicators.”
Not “more AI.”
Not “more dashboards.”

Better ranking. Better sizing. Better discipline.

